  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-05-28T08:01:59.592Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The presence of a Mesh Renderer on the top level or a child of an object with and interaction seems to prevent the highlight from being visible on Quest.\n\nIf a mesh is used that has multiple materials, only the first submesh is highlighted.\n\nIn this example, the horn has three materials, of which the main body is the top submesh. \nOn PC, all the horns highlight the same, using the Mesh Renderer outline where available.  When using just the Mesh Collider, the whole mesh highlights.\n\nOn the Quest, none of the horns with a mesh renderer at or below the Trigger component highlight at all.  Only lone colliders will highlight.  The lone mesh colliders only highlight the horn body submesh.\n\nwrld_69d6ea26-69d2-4eed-bbbe-625b8397c69b",
